  "comment": "**What it does**\nIncome that grows: a decent yield today plus a reliable annual raise, with safety ranked above size of yield.\n- **Your choices:** 2-6% yield (high yield is a warning, not a bonus), 5%+ dividend growth, 5+ year raise streak, 2x FCF coverage, 30-60% payout, profitable only, $2B+, calm-ish, banks and insurers included.\n- Coverage is FCF-based on purpose \u2014 the payout ratio can be flattered by accounting, cash flow can't.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- **This is the tightest block:** `div_payout_ratio` 30-60 cuts the list hard. Widen to 20-70 for noticeably more names.\n- More yield, less safety: raise the yield band's top from 6% to 8%.\n- Longer track record: raise the raise-streak from 5 to 10 years.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- Sort by `income_score`, tiebreak `quality_score`, or `div_coverage` to lead with the safest payouts.\n- Avoid sorting by `growth_score` (not the goal) and raw `div_yield_ttm` (sorting by yield alone puts the riskiest payers on top \u2014 the opposite of this screen's intent).\n\n_Built 2026-08-13 \u00b7 47 matches at build time._",
  "ai_instructions": "Find stocks that pay me a decent dividend today AND raise it every year \u2014 income\nthat grows. Safety over size: I would rather have 3% growing safely than 7% at risk.\n- **Goal**: income (growing). **Dividends**: required \u2014 the whole point.\n- **Yield**: roughly 2-6% \u2014 an unusually high yield is a warning, not a bonus.\n- **Growth**: dividend raised ~5%+ a year, with a raise streak of 5+ years.\n- **Safety first**: the dividend must be covered ~2x by free cash flow, and the\n  payout ratio must sit in the comfortable 30-60% band. Profitable companies only.\n- **Kinds**: normal stocks plus banks and insurance. **Size**: $2B and bigger.\n- **Risk**: calm-ish stocks (no wild movers). **Results**: ~50-200 names.\n- **Sorting**: income first, tiebreak quality.",
